  - conda
  - live-acquisition
  - smart-microscopy
abstract: >-
  The analysis half of ZMART, the microscopy toolkit of the Center for
  Microscopy and Image Analysis (ZMB), University of Zurich. Pipelines are
  YAML pipelines of small Python steps; each step runs in its own conda
  environment inside a worker that stays warm, so analysis keeps pace with
  a microscope that is still acquiring, and steps can be scoped to run once
  per group of images, per compartment or per carrier. Ships two workflows: alignment (focus,
  orientation and the registration of two objectives) and object analysis
  (detection, measurement and population plots).
